  "plan": {
    "hardest_frame": 2,
    "visual_argument": "The state's list parked at one stand-in car per ten listed vehicles in rows of ten bays, so two names fill two long columns and fourteen companies never fill a single row, seen before any numeral is read",
    "build_risk": "315 kit crossovers instanced from one baked model per material with stall bars, wheel stops and a stripe, staged as one subject through a long lens that keeps the horizon; single cars at the far end of the third column must still read at 432 px",
    "distinct_from_recent": "No. 74 was survey lath, a tidal flat and a dark hearing room around one lamp. No. 73 was compute trays in a windowless hall and plan reliefs. No. 72 was a dark lab and plate reliefs. This deck is a parked fleet on asphalt at last light, a count drawn as cars rather than as trays, blocks or plates."
  },
